@startuml
title Semana 5 - Arquitectura Cliente-Servidor y API REST\nCatálogo de Medicamentos

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Cliente\nWeb / Otro módulo" as Cliente

package "Presentation" {
    component "API REST\n/api/v1/medications" as API
    component "MedicationApiController" as ApiController
}

package "Application" {
    component "RegisterMedication" as Register
    component "SearchMedications" as Search
    component "GetMedication" as GetMedication
    component "ToggleMedicationStatus" as Toggle
}

package "Domain" {
    component "Medication" as Medication
    component "MedicationStatus" as Status
    interface "MedicationRepository" as Repository
}

package "Persistence" {
    component "PdoMedicationRepository" as PDORepo
    component "InMemoryMedicationRepository" as MemoryRepo
    component "DatabaseConnection" as DBConnection
}

database "SQLite\nmedications.sqlite" as SQLite

Cliente --> API : HTTP + JSON

API --> ApiController

ApiController --> Register : POST /medications
ApiController --> Search : GET /medications
ApiController --> GetMedication : GET /medications/{id}
ApiController --> Toggle : PATCH /medications/{id}/status

Register --> Repository
Search --> Repository
GetMedication --> Repository
Toggle --> Repository

Register --> Medication
Toggle --> Medication
Medication --> Status

PDORepo ..|> Repository
MemoryRepo ..|> Repository

PDORepo --> DBConnection
DBConnection --> SQLite

note right of API
Contrato REST versionado:
/api/v1

La API recibe y devuelve JSON.
end note

note right of ApiController
No contiene SQL.
No contiene reglas de negocio.
Delega en los casos de uso.
end note

note bottom of Repository
Los casos de uso dependen
del contrato Repository,
no de una tecnología
de persistencia específica.
end note

@enduml